※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4260
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4260 LANG_MASK_NOT_TRUTH_VALUES

※ A mask is one bit for each truth value of a run.  A run of bytes has no one
※ bit per element to give; what is meant is the comparison that makes truth
※ values of it, written inside the call -- `⎕mask(c ≠ 0u8)`.

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let c: u8⟦8⟧ = ⟦1u8, 0u8, 2u8, 0u8, 3u8, 0u8, 4u8, 0u8⟧ in ⎕static
    if ⎕mask(c) = 85u8: 0u6 else: 1u6
